			<div class="content" id="post-content-4798598">
									

<p>Alright, I'm gonna call for an end to this line of discussion - we're not gaining anything from this.</p>
<p>My personal thoughts on Project Crossover aside, there is discussion on the future on that part of the hub, but we have not come up with a definitive course of action to handle this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Why couldn't the SCPfication of characters be non-commercial? I am legitimately confused as to what makes Project Crossover N-C and the rest of the site CC BY-SA 3.0</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Project Crossover is also under the site's license. And considering we're already acknowledging that Project Crossover is a grey area in of itself, this &quot;non-commercial&quot; aspect is less in paper and more in practice: do you really want to be the person who attempts to sell SCPokemon merch, knowing fully well that Nintendo will pursue you over it?</p>

